<title>USA: Great Lakes resumes Dubuque, Iowa service.</title>
<headline>Great Lakes resumes Dubuque, Iowa service.</headline>
<dateline>SPENCER, Iowa 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Great Lakes Aviation, operating as United Express, said Friday it will resume service to Dubuque, Iowa on Tuesday, June 17.</p>
<p>The carrier said it plans to operate four non-stop, round-trip flights a day between Dubuque and Chicago's Ohare Airport.</p>
<p>The resumption of service follows a voluntary suspension on May 16 of all Great Lakes operations.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
